{"text": "If we understand mass culture as a weakening factor of the cultural ties that unite people to their traditions, mass culture weakens the intermediary institutions in society e, g, the family or the school, diminishing their role and overlapping these institutions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example, courts are traditional social institutions and important for the normal and harmonious functioning of collective life. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, when people turn to social networks to put pressure on judicial decisions in certain mediated and politicized processes, this practice is popularized and becomes a habitual form of culture, which is harmful. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Justice must not be done in the public square, which today is converted into a virtual dimension, the social networks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In a democratic state of law, the appropriate place to judge and make justice is the court and in a way that is immune to popular pressure.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "f", " ", "w", "e", " ", "u", "n", "d", "e", "r", "s", "t", "a", "n", "d", " ", "m", "a", "s", "s", " ", "c", "u", "l", "t", "u", "r", "e", " ", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "w", "e", "a", "k", "e", "n", "i", "n", "g", " ", "f", "a", "c", "t", "o", "r", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "u", "l", "t", "u", "r", "a", "l", " ", "t", "i", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "u", "n", "i", "t", "e", " ", "p", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", "i", "r", " ", "t", "r", "a", "d", "i", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", ",", " ", "m", "a", "s", "s", " ", "c", "u", "l", "t", "u", "r", "e", " ", "w", "e", "a", "k", "e", "n", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "i", "n", "t", "e", "r", "m", "e", "d", "i", "a", "r", "y", " ", "i", "n", "s", "t", "i", "t", "u", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "s", "o", "c", "i", "e", "t", "y", " ", "e", ",", " ", "g", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "a", "m", "i", "l", "y", " ", "o", "r", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", 